GTE matrix upload: faithful 18-byte copies in MulMatrix/gte_MulMatrix0/MulMatrix2/ApplyMatrixLV

The binary uploads the 3x3 short matrix into the active GTE rotation registers
with `movsd x4 + movsw` (18 bytes -> 0x74c6f0..0x74c701; e.g. 0x413809 in
gte_MulMatrix0, 0x413d58 in ApplyMatrixLV). Ghidra rendered that as five scalar
assignments through existing symbols: `__globmat = *param_1` -- but __globmat is
SHORT-typed, so only 2 of the 4 source bytes landed and the odd matrix elements
(m01 @0x74c6f2, ...) silently KEPT THE PREVIOUS MATRIX; the final int-typed
store to 0x74c700 wrote 4 bytes where the binary writes 2, clobbering the
translation short @0x74c702.

Observable consequence vs the frozen cold-L9 reference (measured at cf3): the
scene-object pass runs with the leftover object matrix (FUN_004203dc's
param_1==0 path relies on MulMatrix0/ApplyMatrixLV having refreshed the active
matrix); our active row0 was (-1261,-596,-3896) = world row0 with the last car
matrix's m01, vs the reference's pure world (-1261,0,-3896) -> backdrop/tree
scene objects mis-culled (records 0x7846d4/0x784728 never allocated prims, the
~260 missing FT4 quads / black panorama wedges) and every scene object
transformed with a slightly wrong rotation.

